                    "patching_rect": [ 49.0, 19.0, 157.0, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "in 1 (signal) Low Band Input"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "\r\n// 3-band (low/mid/high) summing of crossover signals post processing from an\r\n// upstream \"evi_crossover_3band.gendsp\" / [evi.crossover.3band~]\r\n\r\n// Linkwitz-Rileys sum perfectly flat\r\n\r\nrequire(\"evi_crossovers.genexpr\");\r\n\r\nParam   align(1, min=0, max=1); // 0 = no allpass alignment, 1 = allpass align in this sum (default) ?\r\nParam   order(1, min=0, max=1); // 0 = from 2-pole xover ?, 1 = from 4-pole xover ? (default)\r\npoles   = int(order);\r\nap      = int(align);\r\n\r\n// if using \"evi_crossover_3band.gendsp\" / [evi.crossover.3band~] upstream with it's 'align'\r\n// attribute turned off, you must turn 'align' on in this sum abstraction.\r\n// by default 'align' is on in this sum abstraction because that would be the only point of using it :-).\r\n// apparently allpass alignment should come when summing, but i am not sure this makes much difference ?\r\n\r\nSUM = 0;\r\nif (poles > 0) {\r\n    if (ap > 0) {\r\n        SUM = eviXover4pole3bandSum(in1, in2, in3, in4);  // 4-pole (default)\r\n    } else {\r\n        SUM = in1 + in2 + in3;\r\n    }\r\n} else {\r\n    if (ap > 0) {\r\n        SUM = eviXover2pole3bandSum(in1, in2, in3, in4);  // 2-pole\r\n    } else {\r\n        SUM = in1 + in2 + in3;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\nout1    = SUM;\r\n\r\n// Note: for additional crossovers including 2-band crossovers,\r\n// @see: \"evi_cross.gendsp\" / [evi.cross~] - 4-pole only\r\n// @see: \"evi_crossover.gendsp\" / [evi.crossover~]\r\n// @see: \"evi_crossover_3band.gendsp\" / [evi.crossover.3band~]\r\n// @see: \"evi_crossover_allpass.gendsp\" / [evi.crossover.allpass~]\r\n\r\n",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "maxclass": "codebox",
                    "numinlets": 4,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 49.0, 58.0, 845.0, 646.0 ]
                }
            },
